		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: RD-5R Power Calibration]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4036&amp;p=31188#p31188"><![CDATA[
It's probably accurate enough. Power measurements are difficult to do accurately and also not really very important so I wouldn't worry too much about them. <br><br>It sounds like the minimum your radio can output is 0.28W and the slope is probably not flat below 1W . The firmware power settings below 1W are really just an educated guess as we can't know the exact parameters of every radio.  <br><br>You might get better results by adjusting the 1W calibration to the point where the power just starts to  fall away rapidly. It won't then be exactly 1W but the lower levels might be closer. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Tue May 07, 2024 2:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
